success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"b576593c1e176f0635d3ac9a3207ee85ee82597f92615b29ee96d6e078fef17a"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":337990,"output_tokens":3729,"requests":9}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"4dfdff691d2b010247da6d2f13f5590d43e85c5e2c9d62171e511451c4e4f633"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":269918,"output_tokens":4987,"requests":6}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"0bc0b24801c62b8f3ca42cb861af1548970c1dbde9e7e6de0f4470f104a6459b"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":350429,"output_tokens":3239,"requests":8}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly how the preserved positional (jql, start_at, max_results) signature maps onto the forward-only opaque nextPageToken cursor (e.g. the per-JQL memo accumulates fetched pages and is sliced by start_at:start_at+max_results, walking additional cursor pages only when the requested slice extends past the cached pages), so non-zero and out-of-order start_at calls and the fetcher's offset/stall guards remain correct.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["acli_graph.py get_parent_map docstring: 'there is NO total field and sending startAt is rejected with HTTP 400' and 'paginates via an opaque nextPageToken cursor'","fetch_paging.py:123 `client.search_issues(jql, start_at=start_at, max_results=page_size)` with start_at advancing by page_size each iteration, plus offset-stall detection on page[0]['key'] per offset","Plan Testing names 'out-of-order slice calls' and 'continued active pagination' but the Approach never states the start_at->cursor mapping that makes those slices correct"],"finding":"The plan preserves the search_issues(jql, start_at, max_results) signature but switches the transport to the forward-only /rest/api/3/search/jql endpoint, which (per get_parent_map's documented contract in acli_graph.py) rejects startAt with HTTP 400, exposes no total, and paginates ONLY via an opaque nextPageToken cursor. The plan does not state how a positional start_at/max_results slice maps onto that cursor — the bridge (a per-JQL memo that accumulates fetched pages and is indexed by the slice, fetching more pages lazily when start_at+max_results runs past what is cached) is only implied by 'fetch only enough pages to satisfy the requested slice'. This mapping is load-bearing for mechanism correctness: fetch_paging._iter_pages drives this method with monotonically increasing start_at (0,100,200,...) and the listed 'out-of-order slice calls' test, and fetch_paging also inspects a next_page_token/nextPageToken attribute on the client for its own same-token-twice guard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4fc1e4cd4b1aac06","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Preserve search_issues(jql,start_at,max_results)...Fetch only enough pages to satisfy the requested slice'","norm_id":"n92782cdd5805fb23","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caller (or _iter_pages) requests start_at=100 before start_at=0, or requests a slice past the currently-accumulated pages","fetch_paging reading a next_page_token attribute off the client for its own cursor-stall guard"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that search_issues retains a per-JQL list memo that grows as cursor pages are fetched; a slice request first extends the memo via _iter_cursor_pages until it holds at least start_at+max_results items (or the cursor is exhausted / the fetcher cap halts it), then returns accumulated[start_at:start_at+max_results].","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[non-codebase] Record live bounded-query timing/count evidence, successful merge' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State, per failure arm (HTTP page-read error, malformed-response rejection, cursor-stall), the disposition the caller surfaces using an explicit word (transient/retryable vs fatal/permanent).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.632,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Reject malformed search responses; invalidate a partially failed search so a later attempt cannot silently reuse a truncated result.'","Plan: 'Failed or stalled page reads fail loudly without returning a partial successful result'","ABSENCE: no disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) attached to the HTTP-failure arm, the malformed-response arm, or the cursor-stall arm — the plan states fail-loud + invalidate but not what disposition the caller/bridge surfaces."],"finding":"The plan alters failure/exception semantics (reject malformed responses, fail loudly on HTTP/malformed, invalidate a partially failed search, retry without poisoning) but never states, with an explicit disposition word, what the caller surfaces when a page read fails — i.e. whether an HTTP error or malformed-response is a transient/retryable failure or a fatal/permanent one. Since the pre-fix 120s timeout path drove retryable AWS alarms, masking a retryable transport error as a hard failure (or vice versa) would change the bridge's recovery behavior.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9bb59d29f0f16f8a","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: 'Reject malformed search responses; invalidate a partially failed search...' and Acceptance Criteria line 2 ('Failed or stalled page reads fail loudly without returning a partial successful result')","norm_id":"n9a96c6ce55a37141","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient 5xx/throttle on a page read surfaces as a fatal failure (no retry), so a recoverable transport blip becomes a hard bridge-run failure and re-alarms unnecessarily.","Conversely a malformed/truncated response is treated as retryable and the bridge spins instead of surfacing a permanent fault."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a 'Failure-disposition contract' line: e.g. a transient HTTP/transport error on a page read stays retryable (surfaced so the hourly bridge re-runs); a malformed/truncated response or cursor stall is fatal/permanent for that run and the partial cache is invalidated so no truncated result is reused.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the positive rationale for choosing demand-driven /rest/api/3/search/jql cursor pagination (reuses the one proven cursor walk + its stall semantics, no new backend/dependency/config, and REST first-1000 at ~7s vs the measured 24.4s ACLI --limit 1000) so the fit over the measured alternatives is explicit.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Approach lists mechanism and constraints ('rather than introducing a backend, dependency or configuration') but gives no positive 'this fits because…' statement","Context cites a measured ACLI --limit 1000 at 24.361s and REST first-1000 at 7.047s — evidence that supports a rationale but the Approach never states it"],"finding":"The plan does not state a POSITIVE rationale for why demand-driven cursor pagination over /rest/api/3/search/jql is the right fit for this problem, versus the two obvious alternatives it implicitly passed over (an ACLI --limit flag — the investigation measured 24.361s for --limit 1000, still CLI/timeout-bound; or a new search backend/config knob — which the plan rejects in-line). The Approach section lists WHAT to do (reuse _iter_cursor_pages/_direct_rest_post_json, no new backend/dependency/config) but not WHY that fit beats the measured alternatives.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c3218a2daaaf1bf","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section","norm_id":"n4952265c7a6b0be7","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer or reviewer weighing whether a simpler --limit tweak would suffice"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","